──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHAT WAS SHIPPED
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
A production-polished, Apple-idiomatic UptimeHeatmap at parity with the web source — a rolling N-day
status grid: one tinted square per day (oldest-first), each with a tap popover (date · status label ·
optional summary) and a tier-coloured overall uptime % caption, inside a glass panel, with an optional
footnote.

Faithful-parity branch decision (per the established precedent of the sibling pure-presentational
status primitives HealthRow 0197 and ActiveFilterChips 0147): the web UptimeHeatmap is a PURE
presentational component — it takes `days` / `title` / `footnote` as plain props and renders; it binds
NO data hook, so there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or lose connectivity to. Inventing loading /
error / stale / offline chrome would FABRICATE states the source does not have (a covenant-1 / covenant-3
violation), so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches:
  • data  — one square per day, status fill, tap popover, tier-coloured uptime caption, footnote.
  • empty — zero days (web `days.length === 0` → null uptime, empty grid): heading + footnote still
            render, and the grid region shows a friendly empty state (native HIG — never a blank box).
  • per-square — the five statuses (healthy/degraded/unhealthy/unknown/maintenance) and summary
            present/absent; plus the title override vs. the default heading.
Web-only props className (Tailwind) and id (DOM anchor) have no native peer and are intentionally dropped.

Files (9), all within the prompt's allowed scope (UptimeHeatmap.*):
  UptimeHeatmap.Adapter.swift      — slug, UptimeStatus (web HeroStatus), UptimeDay, UptimeHeatmapInputs,
                                     UptimeHeatmapFormat.percent (web fmtPercent port).
  UptimeHeatmap.Projection.swift   — UptimeTier (web caption ternary), UptimeSquare, UptimeHeatmapProjection
                                     + UptimeHeatmapProjector (uptime arithmetic, square mapping).
  UptimeHeatmap.Model.swift        — UptimeHeatmapStrings (P1/S10 i18n facade), UptimeHeatmapTelemetry
                                     (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default, @Observable UptimeHeatmapModel
                                     (P1/S8), ResolvedUptimeSquare.
  UptimeHeatmap.Views.swift        — status/tier→TSTone (P1/S9), wrapping flow layout (web flex-wrap),
                                     day square + tap popover + macOS hover help, friendly empty state,
                                     content view (TSGlassPanel composition).
  UptimeHeatmap.swift              — public UptimeHeatmap surface (prop init + model/preview/test init).
  UptimeHeatmap.Previews.swift     — operational/high, title+footnote+incidents, outage/low, empty.
  UptimeHeatmap.strings            — P1/S10 catalog: title, caption, 5 status labels, grid + square a11y,
                                     friendly empty.
  UptimeHeatmap.AdapterTests.swift — pure-core XCTest (status, day, inputs, fmt, tier, projector).
  UptimeHeatmap.Tests.swift        — model + tone + views + strings XCTest + telemetry spy.

